# 剩下的只是必要的内边距，不再是"一片空白"。
# [EN] These numbers are the size of the **inner container**, not the dialog size seen on screen —
# [EN] outside it there's also
# [EN] `paper_frame`'s padding/border and `AlertDialog`'s own content padding.
# [EN] Measured (`developers/measure_dialogs.py`):
# [EN] on-screen outer frame width = the width given here + 100
# [EN] It used to be 820, so the outer frame was 920; yet the widest control in each dialog was only
# [EN] 520
# [EN] (the open-book wizard's input box used to be 580, now also reduced to 520) — so about 400px on
# [EN] the right was left blank.
# [EN] Now align directly to control width: **inner = control width 520 → outer frame 620**, content
# [EN] fills it exactly,
# [EN] what's left is only the necessary inner padding, no longer "a blank expanse".
# 高度按内容量分档。**每个对话框内容都带 scroll**，所以给矮了最坏只是滚动，
# 不会把内容裁掉。（注意 `mk_dialog` 里 body 带 `expand=True`，实测会把
# 对话框拉到接近满高 —— 高度这一档还要靠 measure_dialogs 复核。）
# 注意 `paper_frame` 自己还占掉 52px 横向内边距（内层 16×2 + 外层 7×2 + 边框 6）：
# 这里只写 520 的话，控件会把内边距顶掉、内容贴着纸边（实测内容 bbox 距边只剩 4px）。
# 所以宽度 = 控件宽 520 + 52 = 572 → 屏幕上的外框约 620，两侧各留 50px 内边距。
DLG_W = 600          # = 控件宽 520 + 滚动条车道 24 + 纸框内边距 56。

# ── 危险确认框（`_confirm_danger`）的**内容区**高度 ──
# ★★★ 2026-10-14（用户）：「拾卷的删除小说对话框 高度稍微高一些 把输入小说名字的
#   文本框默认漏出来」。
#   实测（`developers/probe_del_dialog.py`，真机量）：
#     · 这个数是**纸框**高，不是内容区高 —— 280 声明下去，渲染出来的**内容区只有
#       186px**（`body` 的实测 bbox 高 186、滚动视口 187）。中间那 94px 是
#       纸框的标题行 + 内边距 + `AlertDialog` 的默认内边距（见 `mk_dialog` 里
#       "即便传 0 仍按默认留白"那条实测）。
#   2026-10-14 第二轮（用户又来了）：「**我不需要每次都动一下滚动条**」——
#   真机用**长书名 + 长路径**复现（`developers/probe_del_dialog_long.py`）：
#     · 短书名（如"判据用书"）自然高 207 ⇒ 够；
#     · **长书名（56 字路径）**自然高 **232** ⇒ 超过可用 ≈206 ⇒ `max=25px`
#       ⇒ 出现 Column 滚动条 ⇒ 用户感受"还要动"。
#   ⇒ 单纯按"短书名够"拍板会把"长书名"漏掉 —— 用户每次都要点的是**他自己
#     的**书，最坏情况才是他看到的"标准场景"。
#   加高：330 → **400**（再加 70 的覆盖：自然高 232 + 余裕 = 380 上下 ⇒ 不滚）。
# [EN] Measured (`developers/probe_del_dialog.py`, real machine):
# [EN]   · This number is **the paper frame's** height, not the content area's -- with 280 declared,
# [EN]     the rendered **content area is only 186px** (body's measured bbox is 186, scroll viewport
# [EN]     187). The 94px in the middle is the paper frame's title row + padding + `AlertDialog`'s
# [EN]     default padding (see the measured "passing 0 still leaves default padding" note in
# [EN]     `mk_dialog`).
# [EN] Second round on 2026-10-14 (the user came again): "I don't need to fiddle with the scrollbar
# [EN] every time" --
# [EN] reproduced on the real machine with **a long book name + long path**
# [ ] (`developers/probe_del_dialog_long.py`):
# [EN]   · Short name (e.g. "判据用书") natural is 207 => enough;
# [EN]   · **Long name (56-char path)** natural is **232** => exceeds usable ~206 => `max=25px`
# [EN]     => Column scrollbar appears => user feels "still have to fiddle".
# [EN]   => Just basing it on "short is enough" misses "long" -- what the user clicks every time is
# [EN]     **his own** book; the worst case is the "standard scene" he sees.
# [EN] Bump it: 330 -> **400** (an extra 70px coverage: natural 232 + slack = ~380, no scroll).
#   ⇒ 两件事一起做才算修好：
#     ① 高度 280 → 330 → **400**：第一轮把 280 抬到 330 是按**短书名**算的（自然高 207），
#        第二轮用**长书名**复现才看到短书名算不到 ⇒ 330 在长书名下自然高 232 仍然
#        要滚 25px ⇒ 再抬 70 ⇒ 400（实测渲染 body = 306、扣 head ≈ 256）覆盖到 232+；
#     ② 手打框**移出滚动区**，钉在底部（见 `_confirm_danger` 里的 `tail`）——
#        只加高度是不够的：书名/路径长短都会让那五行多折一两行，"刚好够"的高度
#        下次又被埋回去。钉在底部才是**结构上的保证** —— 上面多长都露着。
# [EN] => Two things must be done together to really fix it:
# [EN]   ① height 280 -> 330 -> **400**: the first round's 280 -> 330 was tuned for **short names**
# [EN]      (natural 207); the second round's reproduction with **long names** is what exposed the
# [EN]      gap -- 330 still scrolls 25px when natural is 232 => bump another 70 => 400 (rendered body
# [EN]      = 306, minus head ≈ 256), which covers 232+ with slack.
# [EN]   ② move the type-to-confirm box **out of the scroll area**, pinned to the bottom (see
# [EN]      `tail` in `_confirm_danger`) -- raising the height alone is not enough: the book name
# [EN]      length and path length can make those five lines wrap an extra line or two, and an
# [EN]      "exactly enough" height gets buried again next time. Pinning it at the bottom is the
# [EN]      **structural** guarantee -- it stays visible no matter how long the text above is.
